te-parts":[[2009]]},"abstract":"<jats:p>A review of the history and historiography of precious metal coins issued by the caliphal mint of Damascus (72-79 ah) suggests that the caliph's administrators abandoned figurai coinage in favour of epigraphic coinage at the end of the eighth century as the final stage of a series of monetary experiments which aimed to create a universal Islamic coinage type, that would be accepted in all regions of the Umayyad state, including Iran as well as Greater Syria.<\/jats:p>","DOI":"10.3406\/numi.2009.2879","type":"journal-article","created":{"date-parts":[[2014,2,27]],"date-time":"2014-02-27T09:48:32Z","timestamp":1393494512000},"page":"357-381","source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":9,"title":["Abd al-Malik's Coinage Reforms : the Role of the Damascus Mint"],"prefix":"10.3406","volume":"6","author":[{"given":"Luke","family":"Treadwell","sequence":"first","affiliation":[],"role":[{"vocabulary":"crossref","role":"author"}]}],"member":"2000","container-title":["Revue numismatique"],"language":"fr","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2023,1,19]],"date-time":"2023-01-19T12:02:38Z","timestamp":1674129758000},"score":28.963696,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/www.persee.fr\/doc\/numi_0484-8942_2009_num_6_165_2879"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2009]]},"references-count":0,"journal-issue":{"issue":"165","published-print":{"date-parts":[[2009]]}},"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.3406\/numi.2009.2879","ISSN":["0484-8942"],"issn-type":[{"value":"0484-8942","type":"print"}],"published":{"date-parts":[[2009]]}},{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2026,11,11]],"date-time":"2026-11-11T17:34:31Z","timestamp":1794418471002,"version":"4.9.1"},"edition-number":"1","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Cambridge University Press","isbn-type":[{"value":"9781108012249","type":"print"},{"value":"9780511708152","type":"electronic"}],"license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2012,4,5]],"date-time":"2012-04-05T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1333584000000},"content-version":"unspecified"